  "preamble": "Fronting and unrounding of /o/ to /e/. In Latin, the sequence vo- became ve- before s, t and r plus consonant during the 2nd century BC, so that Plautine vortō, voster and vortex gave Classical vertō 'turn', vester 'your' and vertex; inherited Proto-Italic *wors-o- likewise gave verrō 'sweep'. In Albanian, Proto-Albanian long *ō became e by way of a reconstructed diphthong *ue (*trōtja > tres 'to dissolve').",
  "phoneticEffects": "Fronting, Unrounding, Dissimilation",
